@startuml Enterprise_Onboarding_Process
!theme aws-orange
title Процесс настройки многоуровневого BPG для нового предприятия
skinparam linetype ortho

skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor #4169E1
  FontColor black
}

start

' === Phase 1: Initial Assessment ===
partition "📋 Phase 1: Initial Assessment & Setup" {
  :🏢 Enterprise Profile Creation;
  note right
• Company domain (e-commerce, CRM, LMS, etc.)
• Business size and complexity
• Target websites/applications
• User roles and permissions
• Compliance requirements
  end note

  :🌐 Target System Analysis;
  note right
• Website URLs and access credentials
• Authentication requirements
• User permission levels
• System architecture overview
• Integration constraints
  end note

  :📊 Domain Template Pre-selection;
  note right
relevant_templates = template_library.query(
    domain = enterprise_profile.domain,
    complexity = enterprise_profile.complexity,
    industry = enterprise_profile.industry
)

template_recommendations = {
    "entity_templates": relevant_templates.entities,
    "process_templates": relevant_templates.processes,
    "relationship_templates": relevant_templates.relationships,
    "confidence_scores": calculate_applicability_scores()
}
  end note
}

' === Phase 2: Automated Discovery ===
partition "🕷️ Phase 2: Automated System Discovery" {
  :🔍 Systematic Site Crawling;
  note right
crawler_config = {
    "max_pages": 100,
    "crawl_depth": 3,
    "respect_robots_txt": True,
    "authentication": enterprise_profile.auth_config,
    "rate_limiting": "1 request/second"
}

discovered_data = site_crawler.crawl(
    start_urls = target_system.urls,
    config = crawler_config
)

# Results:
# - 45 unique pages discovered
# - 156 UI elements catalogued
# - 23 forms identified
# - 34 navigation patterns extracted
  end note

  :🎨 Multi-modal Analysis;
  note right
**Computer Vision Pipeline:**
• YOLOv8: 156 UI elements detected
• OCR: 89 text elements extracted
• LayoutML: Page structures analyzed
• CLIP: Visual embeddings generated

**Navigation Pattern Discovery:**
• 34 page transition patterns
• 12 user workflow sequences
• 8 authentication flows
• 15 form submission patterns
  end note

  :📊 Page Signature Generation;
  note right
for page in discovered_pages:
    page_signature = generate_signature(
        dom_structure = page.dom,
        ui_elements = page.elements,
        business_purpose = classify_page_purpose(page)
    )

    # Check for similar pages (data variants)
    similar_pages = find_similar_signatures(
        page_signature, existing_pages
    )

    if similar_pages:
        link_as_data_variant(page, similar_pages)
    else:
        create_new_page_template(page)
  end note
}

' === Phase 3: LLM-Enhanced Analysis ===
partition "🧠 Phase 3: LLM-Enhanced Business Analysis" #LightYellow {
  :📄 Business Document Processing;
  note right
LLM Prompt:
"Analyze these business documents for [Company Name]:
- Standard Operating Procedures
- User Training Materials
- Process Documentation

Extract:
1. Business entities (actors, objects, processes)
2. Workflows and decision points
3. Business rules and constraints
4. Success criteria and KPIs

Domain: {enterprise_domain}
Known GUI elements: {discovered_ui_elements}
Format: Structured JSON with confidence scores"
  end note

  :🤖 LLM Entity & Pattern Discovery;
  note right
{
  "discovered_entities": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "category": "Actor",
      "role": "Places orders and makes payments",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "gui_manifestations": ["user profile", "checkout form"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Product",
      "category": "Object",
      "role": "Items available for purchase",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "gui_manifestations": ["product cards", "detail pages"]
    }
  ],
  "discovered_processes": [
    {
      "name": "Order Placement",
      "category": "Transaction",
      "steps": ["Browse", "Select", "Add to Cart", "Checkout"],
      "confidence": 0.89
    }
  ]
}
  end note

  :🎯 Template Matching & Ranking;
  note right
template_matches = []

for discovered_entity in llm_discovered_entities:
    matches = template_library.find_similar_entities(
        entity_description = discovered_entity.description,
        domain_context = enterprise_domain,
        similarity_threshold = 0.7
    )

    for match in matches:
        confidence = calculate_matching_confidence(
            discovered_entity = discovered_entity,
            template = match,
            gui_evidence = discovered_ui_elements,
            business_context = business_documents
        )

        template_matches.append(TemplateMatch(
            discovered_entity = discovered_entity,
            template = match,
            confidence = confidence,
            customization_needed = assess_customization_needs()
        ))
  end note
}

' === Phase 4: Expert Validation ===
partition "👥 Phase 4: Expert Validation & Customization" #LightCoral {
  :📊 Validation Dashboard Generation;
  note right
High Confidence Suggestions (Auto-approve if >0.85):
• Customer entity → EndUser template (0.94)
• Product entity → PurchasableItem template (0.91)
• Order process → TransactionProcess template (0.89)

Medium Confidence (Requires review 0.6-0.85):
• Manager entity → Administrator template (0.78)
• Review process → ApprovalWorkflow template (0.72)

Low Confidence (Manual definition <0.6):
• CustomReportGenerator → No template match (0.34)
  end note

  :🔍 Expert Review Interface;
  note right
Validation UI for Domain Expert:

✅ Approve: Customer → EndUser template
   Customization: Add "loyalty_level" attribute

⚠️ Review: Manager → Administrator template
   Question: Does Manager have approval authority?
   Options: [Yes - keep template] [No - modify template] [Custom entity]

❌ Reject: ProductReview → No good template match
   Action: Create custom entity with attributes:
   - rating: 1-5 scale
   - review_text: free text
   - moderation_status: pending/approved/rejected
  end note

  :🔧 Custom Business Rule Definition;
  note right
custom_business_rules = [
    BusinessRule(
        name = "High Value Order Approval",
        condition = "order.total_amount > 10000",
        action = "require_manager_approval",
        priority = "high",
        validation_method = "human_confirmation"
    ),
    BusinessRule(
        name = "Product Availability Check",
        condition = "product.stock_level < 5",
        action = "display_low_stock_warning",
        priority = "medium",
        validation_method = "automated_check"
    )
]
  end note
}

' === Phase 5: BPG Construction ===
partition "🏗️ **Phase 5: Enterprise BPG Construction**" #Lavender {
  :🎯 Entity Layer Construction;
  note right
enterprise_entities = []

for validated_match in expert_approved_matches:
    enterprise_entity = EnterpriseEntityNode(
        entity_id=generate_uuid(),
        entity_name=validated_match.custom_name,
        template_reference=validated_match.template,
        domain_attributes=validated_match.customizations,
        gui_manifestations=link_to_discovered_elements(
            validated_match.discovered_entity
        ),
        confidence_score=validated_match.final_confidence
    )

    enterprise_entities.append(enterprise_entity)

    # Link to discovered UI elements
    for gui_element in validated_match.gui_elements:
        create_visual_link(
            entity=enterprise_entity,
            ui_element=gui_element,
            link_type="represents"
        )
  end note

  :⚙️ Pattern Layer Construction;
  note right
enterprise_patterns = []

for business_process in validated_processes:
    # Find best matching template
    template_match = find_best_process_template(
        business_process, template_library.process_templates
    )

    enterprise_pattern = EnterprisePatternNode(
        pattern_id=generate_uuid(),
        pattern_name=business_process.custom_name,
        base_template=template_match.template,
        domain_customizations=business_process.customizations,
        involved_entities=link_to_enterprise_entities(
            business_process.required_entities
        ),
        business_rules=custom_business_rules,
        navigation_sequence=extract_navigation_from_discovery(
            business_process, discovered_navigation_patterns
        )
    )

    enterprise_patterns.add(enterprise_pattern)
  end note

  :🔧 Workflow Layer Construction;
  note right
# Generate executable workflows
for enterprise_pattern in enterprise_patterns:
    workflow_nodes = []

    # Decompose pattern into atomic actions
    atomic_actions = decompose_pattern_to_actions(
        pattern=enterprise_pattern,
        atomic_action_templates=template_library.atomic_actions
    )

    for action_template in atomic_actions:
        workflow_node = InteractionWorkflowNode(
            workflow_id=generate_uuid(),
            template_reference=action_template,
            target_elements=[], # Will be linked at runtime
            execution_context=ExecutionContext(
                pattern=enterprise_pattern,
                business_rules=enterprise_pattern.business_rules
            )
        )
        workflow_nodes.add(workflow_node)

    # Link workflow nodes in sequence
    create_workflow_sequence(workflow_nodes)
  end note
}

' === Phase 6: Testing & Optimization ===
partition "🧪 **Phase 6: Testing & Performance Optimization**" #PaleGreen {
  :🔍 BPG Validation Testing;
  note right
test_scenarios = set(
    TestScenario(
        name="Customer Registration Flow",
        user_input="Register new customer John Doe",
        expected_entities=set(["Customer", "RegistrationForm"]),
        expected_patterns=set(["UserRegistrationProcess"]),
        success_criteria="User account created successfully"
    ),
    TestScenario(
        name="Product Purchase Flow",
        user_input="Buy Product X under $50",
        expected_entities=set(["Customer", "Product", "Cart", "Payment"]),
        expected_patterns=set(["ProductSearchProcess", "PurchaseProcess"]),
        success_criteria="Order placed and payment processed"
    )
)

for scenario in test_scenarios:
    test_result = execute_test_scenario(
        scenario=scenario,
        bpg_instance=enterprise_bpg,
        test_environment=staging_environment
    )

    if test_result.success_rate < 0.8:
        identify_failure_points(test_result)
        suggest_optimizations(test_result)
  end note

  :📈 Performance Optimization;
  note right
# Optimize based on test results
optimization_results = dict(
    element_linking_accuracy=0.87,
    pattern_matching_speed="1.2s average",
    workflow_execution_success=0.89,
    required_optimizations=set([
        "Improve element linking cache hit rate to >90%",
        "Optimize navigation pattern matching to <500ms",
        "Enhance cross-view element consistency to >95%"
    ])
)

# Apply optimizations
apply_performance_optimizations(
    enterprise_bpg, optimization_results
)
  end note


  :🎯 A/B Testing Setup;
  note right
# Setup A/B testing for different approaches
nab_test_config = dict(
    test_groups=set([
        dict(name="template_heavy", template_reliance=0.8),
        dict(name="llm_heavy", llm_reliance=0.8),
        dict(name="balanced", template_reliance=0.5, llm_reliance=0.5)
    ]),
    success_metrics=set([
        "workflow_completion_rate",
        "element_linking_accuracy",
        "user_satisfaction_score"
    ]),
    test_duration="2_weeks"
)
  end note

  :📈 Success Metrics & KPIs;
  note right
**📊 Key Success Metrics:**

**Technical Performance:**
• Element linking accuracy: >90%
• Pattern matching speed: <500ms
• Workflow completion rate: >85%
• System uptime: >99.5%

**Business Value:**
• Time-to-value: <2 weeks onboarding
• User adoption rate: >80% within 3 months
• Task automation success: >75%
• Expert time reduction: >60%

**Quality Assurance:**
• False positive rate: <10%
• User satisfaction score: >4.0/5.0
• Business rule compliance: >95%
• Audit trail completeness: 100%
  end note
}

' === Phase 7: Production Deployment ===
partition "🚀 **Phase 7: Production Deployment & Monitoring**" #Moccasin {
  :📊 **Production Readiness Checklist:**

✅ **BPG Quality Metrics:**
• Entity coverage: 95% of discovered entities mapped
• Pattern accuracy: 89% success rate in testing
• Workflow completeness: All critical paths covered
• Performance: <2s average response time

✅ **Security & Compliance:**
• Authentication integration tested
• Data privacy controls implemented
• Audit logging enabled
• GDPR compliance verified

✅ **Monitoring & Alerting:**
• Performance dashboards configured
• Error rate alerting setup
• Usage analytics enabled
• Feedback collection mechanisms active;

  :🔄 Gradual Rollout Strategy;
  note right
rollout_phases = set(
    RolloutPhase(
        name="pilot_users",
        user_percentage=5,
        duration="1_week",
        success_criteria=dict(error_rate="<5%", satisfaction=">4.0")
    ),
    RolloutPhase(
        name="early_adopters",
        user_percentage=25,
        duration="2_weeks",
        success_criteria=dict(error_rate="<3%", satisfaction=">4.2")
    ),
    RolloutPhase(
        name="full_deployment",
        user_percentage=100,
        duration="ongoing",
        success_criteria=dict(error_rate="<2%", satisfaction=">4.3")
    )
)
  end note

  :📈 Continuous Learning Activation;
  note right
# Enable continuous learning pipeline
learning_config = dict(
    feedback_collection=True,
    performance_monitoring=True,
    template_updates=True,
    cross_enterprise_sharing=True, # anonymized
    expert_review_frequency="weekly",
    automated_optimization=True
)

activate_continuous_learning(
    enterprise_bpg, learning_config
)
  end note


  note right
**🔧 Implementation Timeline:**

**Week 1-2: Discovery & Analysis**
• Automated site crawling (3 days)
• LLM business analysis (2 days)
• Template matching (2 days)
• Expert validation sessions (3 days)

**Week 3-4: Construction & Testing**
• BPG construction (5 days)
• Testing and optimization (3 days)
• Security and compliance validation (2 days)

**Week 5-6: Deployment**
• Pilot rollout (1 week)
• Monitoring and adjustments (1 week)

**Ongoing: Optimization**
• Performance monitoring
• Continuous learning
• Template updates
• Cross-enterprise knowledge sharing
  end note
}

stop

' === Resource Requirements ===
legend top
**💼 Resource Requirements for Enterprise Onboarding:**

**Technical Resources:**
• Senior AI/ML Engineer (2-3 weeks)
• Business Process Analyst (1-2 weeks)
